Stack: <%stack%>. Workflow: Ilmarinen <%version%>
(route → blueprint → rune → plan → forge → verify → review → sampo).

## Commands

- `just check` runs every deterministic check; `just check <lang>` scopes it (<%langs%>).
- `just test` runs unit tests; `just e2e` runs end-to-end tests (UI changes).
- `just trace` checks that every Source Reference resolves (writes `artifacts/traceability.md`).
- `just stale` lists Lessons still unpromoted after six weeks; `just retro` prints the trial scorecard.
- `just db-up` / `just db-down` start and remove throwaway local Postgres and SurrealDB.

## Where things are

- `spec/` holds Blueprints (`features/`) and Runes (`decisions/`, `rules/`,
  `lessons/`) in SpecScore format; `specscore spec lint` must pass.
- `docs/` holds human documentation.
- Tasks live in Beads (`bd ready`, `bd create`, `bd update --claim`), never in markdown TODOs.
- Generated output goes to `artifacts/` (gitignored); never treat it as the source of truth.

## Routing

Classify every request before starting: `trivial`, `standard` or `major`.
It is `major` when the word `<%keyword%>` is used, or the change touches an
interface contract, a data model, or more than one repo. State the depth and
the reason in one sentence; never escalate silently; if scope grows, stop and
re-route.

## Source References

- Implementing code: `specscore:implements feature/<slug>#req:<req-slug>`
- Tests: `specscore:verifies feature/<slug>#ac:<ac-slug>`
- Other repos: `specscore://<host>/<org>/<repo>/feature/<slug>#req:<req-slug>`

## Never

- Never read or write `.env*` files.
- Never run a migration against anything but the local throwaway databases (`just db-up`).
- Never force-push.
- Nothing merges without a human.
